    "title": "pandas.IntervalDtype — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.IntervalDtype#\n\n- \nclass pandas.IntervalDtype(*subtype=None* ,*closed=None* )[source]#\n- An ExtensionDtype for Interval data. **This is not an actual numpy dtype** , but a duck type.\n  - Parameters:\n    - **subtype** str, np.dtype\n    - The dtype of the Interval bounds.\n    - **closed** {‘right’, ‘left’, ‘both’, ‘neither’}, default ‘right’\n    - Whether the interval is closed on the left-side, right-side, both or neither. See the Notes for more detailed explanation.\n Attributes `subtype`The dtype of the Interval bounds. Methods **None**See also \n  - `PeriodDtype`\n  - An ExtensionDtype for Period data.\n Examples >>> pd.IntervalDtype(subtype=\"int64\", closed=\"both\") interval[int64, both]",
    "markdown_length": 702,
